166 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 124 0 R/T(MOSHI WAS DEVELOPED AS A HIGH-LEVEL DESIGN AND TECHNOLOGY EXPLORATION USING THE OPEN-SOURCE SESAME ROBOT FRAMEWORK AS A TECHNICAL FOUNDATION.)/E(MOSHI WAS DEVELOPED AS A HIGH-LEVEL DESIGN AND TECHNOLOGY EXPLORATION USING THE OPEN-SOURCE SESAME ROBOT FRAMEWORK AS A TECHNICAL FOUNDATION.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

167 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 125 0 R/T(Project Context)/E(Project Context)/Pg 12 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

168 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 125 0 R/E(TODAY, MOST INTERACTIONS WITH TECHNOLOGY HAPPEN THROUGH SCREENS, MAKING DIGITAL EXPERIENCES INCREASINGLY DETACHED FROM PHYSICAL AND EMOTIONAL ENGAGEMENT. AT THE SAME TIME, ROBOTICS TECHNOLOGY CONTINUES TO ADVANCE RAPIDLY, YET MANY ROBOTIC SYSTEMS STILL FEEL HIGHLY TECHNICAL, INDUSTRIAL, AND INTIMIDATING FOR EVERYDAY USERS.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

169 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 125 0 R/E(MOST AFFORDABLE ROBOTIC PLATFORMS FOCUS HEAVILY ON ENGINEERING FUNCTIONALITY, LOCOMOTION SYSTEMS, AND TECHNICAL PERFORMANCE WHILE LACKING EMOTIONAL ACCESSIBILITY AND INTERACTIVE PERSONALITY. THIS CREATES A DISCONNECT BETWEEN TECHNOLOGICAL CAPABILITY AND HUMAN ENGAGEMENT.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

170 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 125 0 R/E(MOSHI EXPLORES HOW ROBOTICS CAN BECOME MORE EMOTIONALLY APPROACHABLE THROUGH EXPRESSIVE MOVEMENT, BEHAVIORAL INTERACTION, AND PLAYFUL COMMUNICATION SYSTEMS.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

171 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 125 0 R/Pg 12 0 R/A[490 0 R 0]/K[4]>>
endobj

172 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 126 0 R/T(Problem Statement)/E(Problem Statement)/Pg 13 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

173 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 126 0 R/E(MOST EXISTING ROBOTIC SYSTEMS PRIORITIZE FUNCTIONALITY AND TECHNICAL COMPLEXITY OVER EMOTIONAL INTERACTION AND ACCESSIBILITY. AS A RESULT, MANY ROBOTS FEEL MECHANICAL, INTIMIDATING, OR DISCONNECTED FROM EVERYDAY USERS.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

174 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 126 0 R/E(THERE IS AN OPPORTUNITY TO RETHINK ROBOTICS AS EMOTIONALLY ENGAGING COMPANIONS THAT COMMUNICATE THROUGH MOVEMENT, PERSONALITY, AND BEHAVIOR RATHER THAN PURELY UTILITY-DRIVEN MACHINES.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

175 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 126 0 R/E(THE PROJECT INVESTIGATES HOW EXPRESSIVE MOVEMENT, VISUAL COMMUNICATION, AND INTERACTION DESIGN CAN TRANSFORM A ROBOTIC PLATFORM INTO A MORE APPROACHABLE AND RELATABLE EXPERIENCE.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

176 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 126 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/A[491 0 R 0]/K[4]>>
endobj

177 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 127 0 R/T(How might we design a robotic companion that feels emotionally engaging, communicates through expressive behavior, and combines engineering functionality with human-centered interaction design?)/E(How might we design a robotic companion that feels emotionally engaging, communicates through expressive behavior, and combines engineering functionality with human-centered interaction design?)/Pg 14 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

178 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 127 0 R/E(THE GOAL WAS NOT SIMPLY TO BUILD A FUNCTIONING ROBOT, BUT TO EXPLORE HOW ROBOTICS CAN CREATE EMOTIONAL CONNECTION THROUGH MOVEMENT, INTERACTION, AND PERSONALITY.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

179 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 128 0 R/Pg 15 0 R/A[492 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj

180 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 128 0 R/T(Introducing Moshi)/E(Introducing Moshi)/Pg 15 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

181 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 129 0 R/Pg 16 0 R/A[493 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj

182 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 129 0 R/T(OBJECTIVES)/E(OBJECTIVES)/Pg 16 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

183 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(THE PRIMARY OBJECTIVE OF MOSHI WAS TO CREATE AN EMOTIONALLY EXPRESSIVE ROBOTIC COMPANION CAPABLE OF ENGAGING USERS THROUGH MOVEMENT, POSTURE, TIMING, AND VISUAL EXPRESSION.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

184 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(THE PROJECT ALSO AIMED TO EXPLORE HOW INTERACTION DESIGN PRINCIPLES COULD BE INTEGRATED INTO ROBOTICS TO CREATE MORE APPROACHABLE TECHNOLOGICAL EXPERIENCES. FROM A TECHNICAL PERSPECTIVE, THE PROJECT FOCUSED ON DEVELOPING A FUNCTIONAL QUADRUPED LOCOMOTION SYSTEM INTEGRATED WITH EXPRESSIVE OLED-BASED FACIAL ANIMATIONS AND A WIRELESS INTERACTION INTERFACE.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

185 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(ANOTHER MAJOR OBJECTIVE WAS TO TRANSFORM ROBOTICS FROM A CODING-HEAVY ENGINEERING SYSTEM INTO A MORE ACCESSIBLE INTERACTIVE PRODUCT THROUGH BROWSER-BASED CONTROL AND EMOTIONAL COMMUNICATION SYSTEMS.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

186 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 130 0 R/T(Research followed)/E(Research followed)/Pg 17 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

187 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 130 0 R/E(THE RESEARCH PHASE FOCUSED ON UNDERSTANDING HOW HUMANS EMOTIONALLY INTERPRET ROBOTIC BEHAVIOR AND HOW INTERACTION SYSTEMS INFLUENCE ENGAGEMENT WITH TECHNOLOGY.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

188 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 130 0 R/E(RESEARCH AREAS INCLUDED COMPANION ROBOTICS, EMOTIONAL COMPUTING, ANTHROPOMORPHISM, BEHAVIORAL ANIMATION, HUMAN-ROBOT INTERACTION, AND PHYSICAL COMPUTING SYSTEMS. EXISTING ROBOTIC PRODUCTS SUCH AS SONY AIBO, LOVOT, VECTOR, EMO ROBOT, AND PETOI BITTLE WERE STUDIED TO UNDERSTAND HOW MOVEMENT, EXPRESSIONS, AND RESPONSIVENESS INFLUENCE EMOTIONAL PERCEPTION.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

189 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 130 0 R/E(ONE OF THE KEY FINDINGS FROM THE RESEARCH WAS THAT HUMANS NATURALLY ASSIGN PERSONALITY AND EMOTION TO EVEN SIMPLE ROBOTIC BEHAVIORS SUCH AS BLINKING, POSTURE SHIFTS, MOVEMENT TIMING, AND IDLE ANIMATIONS. THIS INSIGHT BECAME ONE OF THE FOUNDATIONAL PRINCIPLES BEHIND MOSHI\220S INTERACTION SYSTEM.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

190 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 130 0 R/Pg 17 0 R/A[494 0 R 0]/K[4]>>
endobj

191 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 131 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/A[495 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj

192 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 131 0 R/T(User Survey)/E(User Survey)/Pg 18 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

193 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(A SMALL USER SURVEY WAS CONDUCTED TO UNDERSTAND HOW USERS EMOTIONALLY PERCEIVE ROBOTIC SYSTEMS AND WHAT QUALITIES MAKE TECHNOLOGY FEEL APPROACHABLE.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

194 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(THE SURVEY EXPLORED QUESTIONS RELATED TO EMOTIONAL INTERACTION, PREFERRED MOVEMENT STYLES, ROBOTIC PERSONALITY, AND VISUAL COMMUNICATION SYSTEMS. MOST PARTICIPANTS PREFERRED EXPRESSIVE EYES AND SUBTLE MOVEMENT OVER REALISTIC HUMANOID FACES OR AGGRESSIVE MECHANICAL MOTION.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

195 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(USERS STRONGLY ASSOCIATED BLINKING WITH AWARENESS, HEAD TILTING WITH CURIOSITY, AND BOUNCING MOVEMENT WITH EXCITEMENT. PARTICIPANTS ALSO PREFERRED SMALLER COMPANION-STYLE ROBOTS OVER INDUSTRIAL ROBOTIC AESTHETICS.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

196 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(THESE FINDINGS DIRECTLY INFLUENCED MOSHI\220S BEHAVIORAL SYSTEM, MOVEMENT LANGUAGE, AND VISUAL DESIGN DIRECTION.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

197 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 131 0 R/T(Concept Development)/E(Concept Development)/Pg 18 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

198 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(THE PROJECT INITIALLY EXPLORED MULTIPLE ROBOTIC ARCHETYPES INCLUDING INDUSTRIAL ROBOTS, FUTURISTIC AI ASSISTANTS, UTILITY ROBOTS, AND PET-INSPIRED COMPANIONS.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

199 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(HOWEVER, THE FINAL DIRECTION FOCUSED ON CREATING A PLAYFUL COMPANION ROBOT INSPIRED BY CAT-LIKE BEHAVIOR AND MOVEMENT. THIS DIRECTION WAS SELECTED BECAUSE FELINE MOVEMENT NATURALLY COMMUNICATES CURIOSITY, CALMNESS, ATTENTIVENESS, AND EMOTIONAL SUBTLETY THROUGH POSTURE AND BEHAVIORAL TIMING.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

200 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(THE CONCEPT SHIFTED THE PROJECT AWAY FROM PURELY TECHNICAL ROBOTICS AND TOWARD A CHARACTER-DRIVEN INTERACTION EXPERIENCE.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

201 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 132 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/A[495 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj

202 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 132 0 R/T(Why cat iteration?)/E(Why cat iteration?)/Pg 19 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

203 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(THE CAT-INSPIRED ITERATION WAS CHOSEN BECAUSE CATS COMMUNICATE EMOTION THROUGH SUBTLE MOVEMENT RATHER THAN EXAGGERATED ACTIONS. THEIR BODY LANGUAGE, BLINKING PATTERNS, POSTURE SHIFTS, AND REACTION TIMING CREATE STRONG EMOTIONAL INTERPRETATION DESPITE MINIMAL MOVEMENT.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

204 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(THIS ALIGNED CLOSELY WITH THE PROJECT GOAL OF EXPLORING EMOTIONAL INTERACTION THROUGH BEHAVIOR-DRIVEN ROBOTICS.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

205 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(THE CAT-INSPIRED VISUAL IDENTITY ALSO HELPED REDUCE ROBOTIC INTIMIDATION BY MAKING THE SYSTEM FEEL SOFTER, MORE FAMILIAR, AND EMOTIONALLY APPROACHABLE. THE EXPRESSIVE FACE DESIGN STRENGTHENED THE CHARACTER IDENTITY OF MOSHI AND ALLOWED THE ROBOT TO FEEL MORE COMPANION-LIKE RATHER THAN MACHINE-LIKE.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

206 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 132 0 R/T(Naming & Identity)/E(Naming & Identity)/Pg 19 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

207 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(THE NAME \215MOSHI\216 WAS SELECTED TO CREATE A SOFT, PLAYFUL, AND EMOTIONALLY WARM IDENTITY FOR THE ROBOT.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

208 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(THE INTENTION BEHIND THE NAME WAS TO MAKE THE ROBOT FEEL APPROACHABLE AND CHARACTER-DRIVEN RATHER THAN PURELY TECHNICAL. THE NAMING ALSO SUPPORTED THE PROJECT\220S LARGER GOAL OF TRANSFORMING ROBOTICS INTO EMOTIONALLY ENGAGING EXPERIENCES.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

209 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(THE VISUAL IDENTITY OF MOSHI COMBINES PLAYFUL GEOMETRY, COMPACT PROPORTIONS, AND EXPRESSIVE DIGITAL FACIAL SYSTEMS TO REINFORCE THE FEELING OF COMPANIONSHIP AND INTERACTION.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

210 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 133 0 R/Pg 20 0 R/A[496 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj

211 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 133 0 R/T(Design Process)/E(Design Process)/Pg 20 0 R/K[1]>>
